NAME
    web-export - export a rendered HTML page while preserving its source behavior

SYNOPSIS
    web-export <http(s)-url> <export-directory>

DESCRIPTION
    Captures a rendered page with the web-analyze Chromium/CDP recorder and
    writes index.html, manifest.json and verified resources under assets/.
    The destination must not already exist. The command prints the absolute
    path to index.html on stdout and sends diagnostics to stderr.

    The captured HTML is retained as the source document. Scripts, inline
    handlers, forms, frames, links, controls, SVG icons and page interactions
    are preserved. The exporter does not add replacement interactions, strip
    scripts, inject a Content-Security-Policy or block network access.

    A reference is changed to a local file only when its exact HTTP(S) URL has
    one unambiguous captured body whose byte size and SHA-256 match recorder
    metadata. HTML src/srcset and resource links (stylesheet, icons, preload
    and related rels) are relinked. Canonical/ordinary links, form actions and
    frame URLs remain source references. CSS url(), @import and image-set()
    references in style attributes, style blocks and captured stylesheet bodies
    are relinked when verified; comments and ordinary string content are kept.
    Changed stylesheets get updated SHA-256 and supported SRI metadata. Script
    source is never modified. Missing, ambiguous, rejected or unverifiable
    resources keep their original URLs and are counted in manifest.json.

    Since source scripts and uncaptured URLs remain active, a page can contact
    its original services and may need a network, authentication or server
    state. The command does not promise that every page is fully offline or
    pixel-identical. It reports what was captured without inventing content
    or interaction behavior.

    Temporary capture data is stored privately and removed after conversion.
    The source capture is not modified.

OPERANDS
    http(s)-url       Absolute HTTP or HTTPS URL to capture.
    export-directory  New destination directory; existing paths are refused.

OUTPUT
    export-directory/
      index.html       Captured HTML with verified resources relinked
      manifest.json    Digests, provenance and coverage/limitation counts
      assets/          Verified captured resource bodies

EXIT STATUS
    0   Export completed. Review manifest.json for resources left remote.
    1   m_ROOT is missing.
    2   m_LIB_DIR is missing.
    3   Invalid operands.
    4   Invalid URL.
    5   Unsupported URL scheme.
    6   Export parent directory could not be created.
    7   Export destination could not be created or already exists.
    8   Browser capture failed.
    9   Capture directory was not reported.
    10  Resource index is unavailable.
    11  Resource index is invalid.
    12  Rendered DOM is unavailable.
    13  Rendered DOM is empty.
    14  Verified captured assets exceed the 512 MiB limit.
    15  Rendered HTML exceeds the 32 MiB limit.
    19  Private temporary capture data could not be removed.
    20  An unexpected export failure occurred.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires an initialized m environment with Node.js, Chromium and
    web-analyze installed. Invoke as `m web-export <url> <directory>`.
